<h1 class="wp-block-heading has-red-color has-white-background-color has-text-color has-background" style="padding-top:0px;padding-right:10px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:10px;font-size:3.7rem">News</h1>
</div></div><div class="stk-separator stk-separator__bottom"><div class="stk-separator__wrapper"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1600 200" class="stk-separator__layer-1" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1610 78.3c-187 54.4-476.7 89.3-802 89.3-334.7 0-631.8-37-818-94.1v136.8h1620v-132z"></path></svg></div></div></div>



<div class="wp-block-stackable-posts stk-block-posts stk--has-container stk-block stk-0df052e is-style-default" data-v="2" data-block-id="0df052e"><div class="stk-inner-blocks stk-content-align stk-0df052e-column"><div class="stk-block-posts__items"><div class="stk-block-posts__item"><div class="stk-container stk-0df052e-container stk-hover-parent"><article><a href="https://cc-ac.org/anurita-chandola-fras-co-designs-sustainable-suits-for-extreme-climates-with-year-5-pupils/" class="stk-block-posts__image-link"><figure class="stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch"><img decoding="async" data-src="https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/DSC_3128-1-1.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image lazyload" alt="" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==" style="--smush-placeholder-width: 7893px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 7893/5262;" /></figure></a><h3 class="stk-block-posts__title"><a href='https://cc-ac.org/anurita-chandola-fras-co-designs-sustainable-suits-for-extreme-climates-with-year-5-pupils/'>Anurita Chandola FRAS Co-designs Sustainable Suits for Extreme Climates with Year 5 Pupils</a></h3><aside class="stk-block-posts__meta stk-subtitle"><time datetime="2026-09-04T09:00:00+01:00">4 September 2026</time></aside><div class="stk-block-posts__excerpt"><p>Anurita Chandola FRAS, a space-wear and textiles artist, recently completed her first co-design project with Year 5 pupils at Charles Dickens Primary School in Southwark, London. Anurita introduced the children to the critical fact that in space, resources are entirely constrained and nothing can be wasted through her brief &#8220;A Sustainable Suit for Extreme Climates&#8221;.</p>
</div><a class="stk-block-posts__readmore has-text-align-center" href="https://cc-ac.org/anurita-chandola-fras-co-designs-sustainable-suits-for-extreme-climates-with-year-5-pupils/">Read more</a></article></div></div><div class="stk-block-posts__item"><div class="stk-container stk-0df052e-container stk-hover-parent"><article><a href="https://cc-ac.org/lande-returns-to-co-design-with-tupton-primary-school-the-farm-of-the-future/" class="stk-block-posts__image-link"><figure class="stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="2058" height="1360" src="https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-09.55.45.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" srcset="https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-09.55.45.png 2058w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-09.55.45-300x198.png 300w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-09.55.45-1024x677.png 1024w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-09.55.45-768x508.png 768w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-09.55.45-1536x1015.png 1536w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-09.55.45-2048x1353.png 2048w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-09.55.45-303x200.png 303w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-28-at-09.55.45-189x125.png 189w" sizes="(max-width: 2058px) 100vw, 2058px" /></figure></a><h3 class="stk-block-posts__title"><a href='https://cc-ac.org/lande-returns-to-co-design-with-tupton-primary-school-the-farm-of-the-future/'>LANDE returns to co-design with Tupton Primary School &quot;The Farm of the Future&quot;</a></h3><aside class="stk-block-posts__meta stk-subtitle"><time datetime="2026-08-06T11:46:19+01:00">6 August 2026</time></aside><div class="stk-block-posts__excerpt"><p>Architect and designer Polly North, founder of LANDE studio, completed her second successful co-design project with CCAC in July called &#8220;Farm of the Future&#8221;.</p>
</div><a class="stk-block-posts__readmore has-text-align-center" href="https://cc-ac.org/lande-returns-to-co-design-with-tupton-primary-school-the-farm-of-the-future/">Read more</a></article></div></div><div class="stk-block-posts__item"><div class="stk-container stk-0df052e-container stk-hover-parent"><article><a href="https://cc-ac.org/ecobots-young-designer-award-winner-luisa-charles-leads-a-climate-robotics-co-design-at-laycock-primary-school/" class="stk-block-posts__image-link"><figure class="stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch"><img decoding="async" width="2560" height="1708" data-src="https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/CCAC_REVEAL_BPC_0201-scaled.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image lazyload" alt="" data-srcset="https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/CCAC_REVEAL_BPC_0201-scaled.jpg 2560w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/CCAC_REVEAL_BPC_0201-300x200.jpg 300w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/CCAC_REVEAL_BPC_0201-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/CCAC_REVEAL_BPC_0201-768x512.jpg 768w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/CCAC_REVEAL_BPC_0201-1536x1025.jpg 1536w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/CCAC_REVEAL_BPC_0201-2048x1366.jpg 2048w, https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/CCAC_REVEAL_BPC_0201-187x125.jpg 187w" data-sizes="(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==" style="--smush-placeholder-width: 2560px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 2560/1708;" /></figure></a><h3 class="stk-block-posts__title"><a href='https://cc-ac.org/ecobots-young-designer-award-winner-luisa-charles-leads-a-climate-robotics-co-design-at-laycock-primary-school/'>Ecobots: Young Designer Award Winner Luisa Charles Leads a Climate-Robotics Co-design at Laycock Primary School </a></h3><aside class="stk-block-posts__meta stk-subtitle"><time datetime="2026-07-16T14:55:56+01:00">16 July 2026</time></aside><div class="stk-block-posts__excerpt"><p>Luisa Charles, a multi-award-winning interactive design engineer and one of CCAC’s Young Designer Award winners of 2025, has successfully completed her first co-design.</p>
</div><a class="stk-block-posts__readmore has-text-align-center" href="https://cc-ac.org/ecobots-young-designer-award-winner-luisa-charles-leads-a-climate-robotics-co-design-at-laycock-primary-school/">Read more</a></article></div></div><div class="stk-block-posts__item"><div class="stk-container stk-0df052e-container stk-hover-parent"><article><a href="https://cc-ac.org/hassell-returns-to-co-design-with-the-children-at-st-johns-and-st-clements-primary-school-peckham/" class="stk-block-posts__image-link"><figure class="stk-img-wrapper stk-image--shape-stretch"><img decoding="async" data-src="https://cc-ac.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/DSC_3318-1-1.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image lazyload" alt="" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==" style="--smush-placeholder-width: 8071px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 8071/5381;" /></figure></a><h3 class="stk-block-posts__title"><a href='https://cc-ac.org/hassell-returns-to-co-design-with-the-children-at-st-johns-and-st-clements-primary-school-peckham/'>Hassell Returns to Co-Design with the Children at St John’s and St Clement’s Primary School, Peckham  </a></h3><aside class="stk-block-posts__meta stk-subtitle"><time datetime="2026-07-07T14:04:59+01:00">7 July 2026</time></aside><div class="stk-block-posts__excerpt"><p>Michael Pecirno, Sustainable Futures Lead at Hassell, recently completed his third successful CCAC co-design project &#8211; his second with Year 5 at St John’s and St Clement’s Primary School. </p>
